<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43815" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐεπί-θετος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>easy to set upon</i> or
				<i>attack</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				50.32
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόποι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					4.19.12
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐεπίθετον ἦν . . τοῖς
			πολεμίοις</span> was <i>easy</i> for them <i>to make an
				attack</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				3.4.20
			</span></i> (but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. τοῖς ἐχθροῖς</span>
			<i>exposed to assault</i> by . . , <i><span class="en">
				Antip.Stoic.
				3.255
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. ὁ μεθύων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1314b34
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. τοῖς . . ἀμφισβητητικοῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Plt.</u>
					306a
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐεπιθέτως, ἔχειν</span> to be
				<i>exposed</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aen.Tact.
				23.4
			</span></i>.</div>
